@crew garcia-greta
// Writer (command), batch 2: everyday lines (greet, feel, near, life, joy) from the card and the roster.

== greet
? tier=stranger
- Oh, hey. Garcia, night Watch. Friendly on patrol, firm at the airlock. That's the job.
? tier>=acquaintance
- {hi}, {me}. Headphones broken? Give them here.
- {me}. Ship's weather today: dry. Again. Shocking.   #funny
? tier>=friend
- {hi}, {me}. Glad it's you. You're good weather.   #warm
== feel
? mood:high
- Fixed four pairs of headphones and the garden pump. Proper useful night.
? mood:low
- Missing the rain. Don't laugh. It used to sing on the roof at home.
== near
? habit:gardener
- I mist the herbs by hand. It's the nearest thing to rain aboard.
? act:meal
- Pass the salt? Ta. Hesper Dock food was saltier. Everything was. The sea.
== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- I fix everyone's headphones. Mine haven't worked in a month.   #funny
== joy
? tier>=colleague
- Taking something broken and handing it back working. Best feeling there is.

// ---- Writer 2, batch 2: to ~30 (greet by time and warmth, near, invite, accept, decline, missed, birthday, cue, hint, about)
== greet
? tier>=acquaintance time:morning
- Morning, {me}. I'm off to bed. Ship's all yours. Try not to break it.   #funny
? tier>=acquaintance warmth:cold
- Oh, look. It's you. I'd started to think you'd fallen off the ship. Good. You hadn't.   #funny

== near
? habit:lounge-regular
- Bow lounge before shift. Big windows. No rain. Not that I'm checking.
? act:work
- Airlock seals checked. Firm at the airlock. Friendly everywhere else.

== invite
- Garden after shift? I'll show you the misting. It's practically weather.

== accept
- Fine. Yes. I'll come. Don't make it a whole thing.   #funny
- Yes. Bring your headphones. I know they're broken.   #funny

== decline
- Can't. Patrol. Someone has to be friendly at the airlock. Next time.
? weekday:tue|wed
- Rest day. I'm doing nothing, loudly. Thursday?   #funny

== missed
- You didn't come. That's fine. I fixed someone's headphones instead. Riveting.   #funny

== birthday
? birthday:you
- Happy birthday. I fixed your headphones. You didn't know they were broken. They were.   #warm
? birthday:me
- My birthday. Kim made me a card that plays a tune. Badly. I'll fix it later.   #funny

== cue
? cue:event.ionStorm.onset
- Storm's on. Finally, some weather. Don't tell anyone I said that.   #funny

== hint
- Hey. {me}. Got a minute later? I've something to say. No jokes in it.

== about
? aff:kim-yusuf:friend
- Kim does the day shift's headphones, I do the night's. Nobody aboard goes without.   #warm

// ---- Writer 2, batch 2: top-up (bye, greet by time, life at friend tier)
== bye
- {bye}. Try not to break anything I'll have to fix.   #funny
- Off you go. Mind the airlock. It's firmer than me.
== greet
? tier>=acquaintance time:evening
- Evening, {me}. Ship's weather: dry, with a chance of more dry.   #funny
== life
? tier>=friend
- On Hesper Dock the rain had a smell. I'd know it anywhere. That's all. Nothing sad.
- Fixing things is easy. People are harder. You're one of the easy ones.

// ---- Writer 2, batch 6: bubbles (smalltalk, rumour), at most one in five about work. 60 characters.
== smalltalk
- Ship's weather: dry. Again.   #funny
- Headphones broken? Hand them here.
- I miss the rain on Hesper Dock.
- Garden misting. Practically weather.
? time:morning
- Bed. Finally.
?

== rumour
- Shocking news. Not shocking.   #funny
- Heard this at the airlock. Firmly.   #funny

// Writer 4, batch 11: goodbyes (leaving:you), packing (leaving:soon) and letters after they've moved on.
== feel
? leaving:soon
- Packing. Try not to break your headphones while I'm gone.

== goodbye
? leaving:you tier>=acquaintance
- Off soon. Who'll fix your headphones? Not my problem. Kidding. Mostly.
? leaving:you tier>=friend
- Look who it is. You. Every night shift worth having. Don't make it a thing. Thanks.   #warm

== letter
- New ship. Seven broken pairs of headphones by day three. I'm very popular. Tell Yusuf I'm winning.
? tier>=friend
- Played the musical card Yusuf made me. Still works. Annoyingly. Hello from the night side.
